    "display(Image(\"figures/scMae0.png\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a5f5c901-0133-4e80-a404-39eda59771dd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Real scRNA-seq data analysis results. (A) [ARI](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.adjusted_rand_score.html) scores of scMAE and seven comparative methods on 15 real scRNA-seq datasets. Each block represents the performance of a method on a dataset, where the size indicates the ARI score and the color represents the rank. The last column shows the average ARI score of each method. (B) Bar plots showing the average ARI values on the 15 real scRNA-seq datasets using scMAE and seven comparative methods. (C) Bar plots showing the average [NMI](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.normalized_mutual_info_score.html) values on the 15 real scRNA-seq datasets using scMAE and seven comparative methods. (D) UMAP visualization of the cell embeddings for [Macosko datasets](https://singlecell.broadinstitute.org/single_cell/study/SCP2158/macosko-mouse-brain-atlas-single-nuclei-dataset?scpbr=biccn-anatomy-and-morphology-project) learned by scMAE and comparative methods. The colors represent the clustering labels of each method. (E) UMAP visualization of the cell embeddings for Macosko datasets learned by scMAE and comparative methods. The colors represent the true cell types."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 202,
   "id": "12fbcf8c-6149-47f2-b28c-91b7b9382a08",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import scanpy as sc\n",
    "import h5py\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import argparse"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1de500db-8024-4a25-b7b6-f9301d07546f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Accessing single-cell data\n",
    "\n",
    "- Melanoma dataset (Metastatic melanoma): Melanoma is a kind of skin cancer that starts in the melanocytes. Melanocytes are cells that make the pigment that gives skin its color. The pigment is called melanin.\n",
    "- Download data from [Zenodo](https://zenodo.org/deposit/8175767)\n",
    "- These are HDF5 stores containing single-cell gene expression datasets along with their cell types. > 4500 single cells isolated from 19 patients, profiling malignant, immune, stromal, and endothelial cells.\n",
    "- Number of cells: 4513, number of genes: 23684, number of cell types: 9\n",
    "- Dataset from [publication](https://www.weizmann.ac.il/mcb/tirosh/sites/mcb.tirosh/files/uploads/Tirosh_Dissecting_the_melanoma_ecosystem.pdf)\n",
    "- Cell types: ['B cell', 'CD4+ T cell', 'Endothelial cell', \"NK cell\", \"Tumor\", \"Unknown\", \"CAF\", \"CD8+ T cell\", \"Macrophage\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 203,
   "id": "89bf5c89-fa71-46ea-94d8-0f212908aade",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "## Download this dataset by uncommenting\n",
    "#import requests\n",
    "#local_data_path = \"data/Melanoma_5K.h5\"\n",
    "#sc_data_zenodo = \"https://zenodo.org/records/8175767/files/Melanoma_5K.h5?download=1\"\n",
    "#r = requests.get(sc_data_zenodo, allow_redirects=True)\n",
    "#open(local_data_path, 'wb').write(r.content)'''"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 204,
   "id": "29ac13fe-67c8-4177-aa9c-4559f303aef3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
