  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fc5c2b55-0099-40bb-bdfc-ae9db950d82b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell types\n",
    "\n",
    "- B cell: A type of lymphocyte (white blood cell) that is part of the adaptive immune system. B cells are responsible for producing antibodies that help to neutralize pathogens.\n",
    "\n",
    "- CAF (Cancer-associated fibroblast): Fibroblasts associated with tumors that play a role in the tumor microenvironment, supporting tumor growth, invasion, and metastasis. They are not immune cells but interact with immune and tumor cells.\n",
    "\n",
    "- CD4+ T cell: A subtype of T lymphocytes (T helper cells) that are crucial for immune signaling. They \"help\" by coordinating the immune response and are essential in adaptive immunity.\n",
    "\n",
    "- CD8+ T cell: A subtype of T lymphocytes (cytotoxic T cells) that are responsible for directly killing infected or cancerous cells. They recognize and destroy cells presenting specific antigens.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Endothelial cell: These cells line blood vessels and are essential for vascular function. They play roles in nutrient exchange, blood flow, and immune cell trafficking within tissues.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Macrophage: A type of immune cell responsible for phagocytosis (engulfing and digesting pathogens and debris) and presenting antigens to T cells. They are involved in inflammation and tissue repair.\n",
    "\n",
    "- NK cell (Natural Killer cell): Part of the innate immune system, NK cells can recognize and kill cells that are stressed, infected, or cancerous without prior sensitization to specific antigens.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Tumor cell: Cancerous cells within a tumor that have acquired mutations leading to uncontrolled growth and the ability to evade normal cellular regulations.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Unknown: Cells that have not been classified or identified, possibly due to insufficient markers or ambiguous characteristics in the dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 206,
   "id": "c4289db7-650e-454d-a74b-ef96c15f98db",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "display(Image(\"figures/anndata.png\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "184b8154-7732-4df3-a5eb-31b5dabfdd4e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Key Features of AnnData\n",
    "- Structured Data Storage: AnnData provides a structured way to store both the main data matrix (e.g., gene expression counts) and the associated metadata, which includes information about cells, genes, experimental conditions, and other annotations.\n",
    "\n",
    "- HDF5-Based Storage: It is built on top of the h5py and anndata libraries, allowing efficient memory management and disk storage. This is especially useful for large single-cell datasets, as data can be stored in HDF5 format to save memory.\n",
    "\n",
    "Main Components:\n",
    "\n",
    "- X: The main data matrix, typically holding the gene expression values. The rows usually represent cells, and the columns represent genes.\n",
    "- obs: Stores metadata for the cells (rows of the data matrix), such as cell type labels, clustering information, or patient/sample information.\n",
    "- var: Stores metadata for genes (columns of the data matrix), such as gene names, annotations, or gene-specific information."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 207,
   "id": "86076f84-a071-47cc-b747-20d5fd4bb131",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "display(Image(\"figures/scanpy.png\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8f54c537-8ac2-4e16-8e4f-0125a2b5bcfc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "- Data normalisation\n",
    "- Data imputation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data filtering and normalisation (ScanPy)\n",
    "\n",
    "- Filter genes - keep genes that have at least `min_counts` counts  - `sc.pp.filter_genes()`\n",
    "- Filter cells - filter cell outliers based on counts - `sc.pp.filter_cells()`         \n",
    "- Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data can vary greatly in sequencing depth across cells, leading to differences in total counts that are not biologically meaningful. Normalization scales the data so that each cell has the same total count to make data from different cells comparable.\n",
    "- Normalize each cell by total counts over all genes, so every cell has the same total count after normalization. If a cell initially has a total expression count of 50,000 and target_sum=1e4, each gene's counts will be scaled down by a factor of 5 (i.e., 50000/10000 = 5). This ensures that all cells in the dataset have comparable total counts after normalization, facilitating downstream analysis such as clustering or differential expression testing - `scanpy.pp.normalize_total()`\n",
    "- Highly variable genes - `sc.pp.highly_variable_genes()`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0d9b95b2-a0c8-4677-821d-8fc162ca062d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Data imputation using TruncatedSVD"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 208,
   "id": "ca167f7e-b90c-4387-9854-aa0d37456ed1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "display(Image(\"figures/svd.png\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a8ce0d4c-0d36-4c4c-a29c-280fb529d3d8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- SVD - Singular value decomposition - factorisation of matrix A into a product of 3 matrices\n",
    "- A is M x N matrix\n",
    "- U is an M √ó M orthogonal matrix whose columns are the left singular vectors of A\n",
    "- D is an M √ó N diagonal matrix whose diagonal elements are the singular values of A, arranged in descending order\n",
    "- V.T is an N √ó N orthogonal matrix whose rows are the right singular vectors of A.\n",
    "- Properties of SVD\n",
    "  - Orthogonality: U and V are orthogonal matrices, meaning U.T x U = I or U x U.T = I and V.T x V = I or V x V.T = I\n",
    "  - Singular Values: The diagonal elements of D are non-negative real numbers, called the singular values of A. They indicate the amount of variance captured by each singular vector.\n",
    "\n",
    "- TruncatedSVD - Take first k columns of U, D(k x k, top k singular values) and first k rows of V."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 209,
   "id": "bd590c1d-906a-41da-b532-dbe1fa8c55c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "display(Image(\"figures/svdex1.png\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 210,
   "id": "f38f4413-66c7-4b59-bd74-6f858cd9d0fb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "display(Image(\"figures/svdex2.png\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "64a55ce1-aa86-467e-a9ae-90e122720a21",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### For Compact SVD\n",
    "- Take first r (r is matrix's rank) columns of U, r x r from singular values, and first r rows from V.T or V*\n",
    "### For Truncated SVD\n",
    "- Take first k (r is matrix's rank) columns of U, k x k from singular values, and first k rows from V.T or V* where k << r"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 211,
   "id": "8251e049-a3fb-4cff-a27f-ddd4b397c6f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import scanpy as sc\n",
    "import h5py\n",
    "import scipy as sp\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, Dataset\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, Markdown\n",
    "\n",
    "default_svd_params = {\n",
    "    \"n_components\": 128,\n",
    "    \"random_state\": 42,\n",
    "    \"n_oversamples\": 20,\n",
    "    \"n_iter\": 7,\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "encoder_x = LabelEncoder()\n",
    "celltypes_keys = dict()\n",
    "\n",
    "class IterativeSVDImputator(object):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, svd_params=default_svd_params, iters=2):\n",
    "        self.missing_values = 0.0\n",
    "        self.svd_params = svd_params\n",
    "        self.iters = iters\n",
    "        self.svd_decomposers = [None for _ in range(self.iters)]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def fit(self, X):\n",
    "        mask = X == self.missing_values\n",
    "        transformed_X = X.copy()\n",
    "        for i in range(self.iters):\n",
    "            self.svd_decomposers[i] = TruncatedSVD(**self.svd_params)\n",
    "            self.svd_decomposers[i].fit(transformed_X)\n",
    "            new_X = self.svd_decomposers[i].inverse_transform(\n",
    "                self.svd_decomposers[i].transform(transformed_X))\n",
    "            transformed_X[mask] = new_X[mask]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def transform(self, X):\n",
    "        mask = X == self.missing_values\n",
    "        transformed_X = X.copy()\n",
    "        for i in range(self.iters):\n",
    "            new_X = self.svd_decomposers[i].inverse_transform(\n",
    "                self.svd_decomposers[i].transform(transformed_X))\n",
    "            transformed_X[mask] = new_X[mask]\n",
    "        return transformed_X"
   ]
  },
